{# IN·03 — where every incident was filed.

   THE MAP IS THE ATLAS'S. This module states what is on it in PHP
   (Service/IncidentMapService) and calls render_map(); the imagery, the
   boundary treatment, the control stack, the legend and fullscreen are the
   platform's, so an incident map, a patrol map and the area map cannot disagree
   about any of them. The module writes no map JavaScript.

   THE MARKS MEAN SOMETHING, and the legend says what: one layer per category in
   that category's own hue, each row a switch. The area's zones lie underneath,
   quiet, wearing their names.

   THE FILTER ROW RIDES IN THE PLATE, one row above the map, so the chips stay a
   row in fullscreen instead of being left behind on the page. #}
<div class="c" data-w="map">
    <span class="tab">Incident map<span class="src">· one filter drives map AND list</span></span>
    {% set filters %}{{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/dashboard/_filters.html.twig') }}{% endset %}
    {{ render_map(dashboard.map, {'role': 'img', 'aria-label': 'Where every incident was filed'}, filters) }}
</div>
